NOTICE - British Isles accents (aiva-isles)

Source material
---------------
Dataset: ylacombe/english_dialects (https://huggingface.co/datasets/ylacombe/english_dialects)
License: CC-BY-SA-4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)

The dataset is a Hugging Face re-publication of the Google crowdsourced
high-quality English dialect speech corpora (Scottish, Welsh, Northern, Midlands
and Southern English, and Irish English), released through OpenSLR
(https://www.openslr.org/83/). If you use these voices in published work, please
cite the original corpus paper:

  Isin Demirsahin, Oddur Kjartansson, Alexander Gutkin, Clara Rivera.
  "Open-source Multi-speaker Corpora of the English Accents in the British
  Isles." Proceedings of the 12th Language Resources and Evaluation Conference
  (LREC 2020), pp. 6532-6541.

The recordings were made by volunteer speakers. No speaker is named in this
pack; voices are labelled only by region and sex.

Derivative material (changes made)
----------------------------------
The files in this pack are adaptations of that dataset, not copies of it:

  style/*.npy    Kokoro-82M style tensors (510 x 1 x 256, float32). Each one was
                 found by a random search (KVoiceWalk, Apache-2.0) that adjusts a
                 tensor until Kokoro speech sounds as similar as possible to one
                 dataset speaker, measured by a speaker-embedding similarity. The
                 tensor is a numeric derivative of that speaker's recordings.
  clips/*.wav    Excerpts of the speaker's recordings (whole sentences, at most
  clips/*.txt    10 seconds), resampled to 24 kHz mono, trimmed of silence and
                 level-normalised. The .txt next to each clip is the sentence
                 text from the dataset.
  preview/*.wav  Short samples generated by Kokoro-82M using the style tensor.

Because the sources are CC-BY-SA-4.0, these derivatives are shared under the same
license; see LICENSE. All voices are marked "experimental": they were checked
only by short listening tests and by the similarity score during the search, and
they imitate an accent loosely rather than reproduce a person.

Other components
----------------
Kokoro-82M (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) generates the previews and consumes the tensors.
KVoiceWalk (RobViren/kvoicewalk, Apache-2.0) is the search tool; the regeneration
scripts live in tools/voicepack of the AIVoiceActing repository.
